markovBases -- all minimal Markov bases of a configuration matrix
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        K = markovBases A
        L = markovBases(A, R)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, configuration matrix
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, ring with one generator for each
        column of $A$
  * Outputs:
      * K, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the minimal Markov bases A
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, ideals in R generated by the
        minimal Markov bases of $A$

Description
===========

This method produces all minimal Markov bases of a given configuration matrix
$A \in \ZZ^{d \times n}$. By default, the output is formatted in the same way
as *note toricMarkov: (FourTiTwo)toricMarkov,: each Markov basis is a $k \times
n$ matrix whose rows correspond to the elements of the Markov basis.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : netList markovBases matrix "3,4,5" -- unique Markov basis|
|                                                              |
|     +-----------+                                            |
|o1 = || 1 -2 1  ||                                            |
|     || 3 -1 -1 ||                                            |
|     || 2 1  -2 ||                                            |
|     +-----------+                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : netList markovBases matrix "1,2,3"                       |
|                                                              |
|     +-----------+                                            |
|o2 = || 2 -1 0  ||                                            |
|     || 1 1  -1 ||                                            |
|     +-----------+                                            |
|     || 2 -1 0  ||                                            |
|     || 3 0  -1 ||                                            |
|     +-----------+                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : netList markovBases matrix "1,2,3,4"                     |
|                                                              |
|     +--------------+                                         |
|o3 = || 2 -1 0  0  ||                                         |
|     || 1 1  -1 0  ||                                         |
|     || 0 2  0  -1 ||                                         |
|     +--------------+                                         |
|     || 2 -1 0  0  ||                                         |
|     || 1 1  -1 0  ||                                         |
|     || 1 0  1  -1 ||                                         |
|     +--------------+                                         |
|     || 2 -1 0  0  ||                                         |
|     || 1 1  -1 0  ||                                         |
|     || 2 1  0  -1 ||                                         |
|     +--------------+                                         |
