toricIndispensableSet -- the indispensable set of toric binomials
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = toricIndispensableSet A
        I = toricIndispensableSet(A, R)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the configuration matrix
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, with one generator for each
        column of $A$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ReturnFiberValues => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether to return the fibers of indispensable
        binomials
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, indispensable set of toric
        binomials
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in $R$ generated by
        the indispensable binomials

Description
===========

A binomial $x^u - x^v$ of a toric ideal $I_A$ is called indispensable if it
belongs to every minimal Markov basis of A. The set of all indispensable
elements is called the indispensable set, and is often denoted with $S(A)$.

This method computes the indispensable set of a matrix $A$ and returns the
indispensibles as the rows of a matrix. Similarly to *note markovBases:
markovBases,, if a ring $R$ is supplied, then the result is an ideal generated
by the indispensable set.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix "7,8,9,10";                                      |
|                                                                 |
|              1       4                                          |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : toricIndispensableSet A                                     |
|                                                                 |
|o2 = | 0 1  -2 1  |                                              |
|     | 1 -2 1  0  |                                              |
|     | 1 -1 -1 1  |                                              |
|     | 3 1  -1 -2 |                                              |
|                                                                 |
|              4       4                                          |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : toricIndispensableSet(A, QQ[x_1 .. x_4])                    |
|                                                                 |
|               2            2                         3        2 |
|o3 = ideal (- x  + x x , - x  + x x , - x x  + x x , x x  - x x )|
|               3    2 4     2    1 3     2 3    1 4   1 2    3 4 |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                                         |
|                  1   4                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

If the optional argument ReturnFiberValues is set to true, then the function
instead returns the list of fibers of the indispensable binomials.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : toricIndispensableSet(A, ReturnFiberValues => true)|
|                                                        |
|o4 = {{18}, {16}, {17}, {29}}                           |
|                                                        |
|o4 : List                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

The function computes the indispensable elements by checking the connected
components of the fiber graph of $A$; see *note fiberGraph: fiberGraph,. A
fiber gives rise to an indispensable element if and only if it has exactly two
connected components and each component contains a single a single point in the
fiber.

See also
========

  * *note markovBases: markovBases, -- all minimal Markov bases of a
    configuration matrix
  * *note fiberGraph: fiberGraph, -- generating fibers of a configuration
    matrix

Ways to use toricIndispensableSet:
==================================

  * "toricIndispensableSet(Matrix)"
  * "toricIndispensableSet(Matrix,Ring)"
  * toricIndispensableSet(Matrix,Matrix) (missing documentation)

For the programmer
==================

The object *note toricIndispensableSet: toricIndispensableSet, is a *note
method function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

